<PageLayout title="Affiliate Disclosure" description="Sublime Pantry's affiliate and material-connection disclosure: what exists today (nothing) and how future relationships will be disclosed." path="/affiliate-disclosure">
  <span class="kicker">Policy</span>
  <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>
  <p><strong>As of August 31, 2026, Sublime Pantry has no affiliate relationships, sponsorships, or paid placements.</strong> No link on this site earns us money.</p>
  <h2>What will change, and how you'll know</h2>
  <p>We expect to add affiliate relationships in the future — most likely for freeze dryers and packaging supplies. When we do:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Affiliate links will be marked with <code>rel="sponsored"</code> and disclosed clearly <em>on the page and near the link</em>, not only here.</li>
    <li>A commercial relationship will never change a comparison's criteria or conclusions; the criteria are published before the products are scored.</li>
    <li>If we ever sell our own product in a category we cover, that ownership will be disclosed prominently on every page that mentions it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This approach follows the FTC's Endorsement Guides, which require material connections to be disclosed clearly and conspicuously near the recommendation. We also do not publish fake or AI-generated reviews or testimonials — the FTC prohibits them, and so do our <a href="/editorial-standards">editorial standards</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
